# THE DATA LEMMA, DATE-TIME HALF (SPEC.md §5.2; issue #135), SPDX-shaped: the
# SPDX 3.0.1 core:created pattern. :created is an xsd:dateTimeStamp property and
# :issued an xsd:dateTime property, both asserted only with valid date-time
# literals on named individuals, and each assertion lies in its range. So both
# properties are literal-asserted, and their assertions and ranges are inert in
# every rung. :issued carries a no-timezone value, 2024-02-29T24:00:00 (a valid
# XSD 1.1 end-of-day in a leap year), and a timezoned one. :A and :B are
# disjoint, :C is a subclass of :A, and :D is unrelated, so the verdict is
# COHERENT (exit 0) with nothing omitted.

@prefix :     <https://example.org/> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class . :D a owl:Class .
:C rdfs:subClassOf :A .
:A owl:disjointWith :B .

:created a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "The date and time at which the element was created." ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTimeStamp .
:issued a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime .

:j a :C ; :created "2024-11-22T03:00:01Z"^^xsd:dateTimeStamp .
:k a :B ; :created "2024-11-23T10:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTimeStamp .
:l a :D ; :created "2024-11-22T03:00:01Z"^^xsd:dateTimeStamp .

:j :issued "2024-02-29T24:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .
:k :issued "2024-02-29T12:00:00+05:00"^^xsd:dateTime .
